  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef's phone has a battery level of NNN percent.\n\nEach minute:\n\n\nIf the phone is on charging, the battery level **increases** by 2%2\\%2%.\nOtherwise, the battery level **decreases** by 3%3\\%3%.\nFind the **minimum** time in which Chef can make the battery level reach **exactly** 50%50\\%50%.\n\nNote that the battery level should always lie in the range 000 to 100100100 (both included).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of single lines of input NNN - the current battery level of Chef's phone.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the **minimum** time in which Chef can make the battery level reach **exactly** 50%50\\%50%.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "0≤N≤1000 \\leq N \\leq 1000≤N≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n51\n50\n23\n0",
        "output": "2\n0\n16\n25",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Chef can use his phone for 111 minute. Thus, the battery drops to 48%48\\%48%.\nThen, he can charge it for 111 minute. Thus, the battery reaches exactly 50%50\\%50%.\nTest case 222: The battery level is already at 50%50\\%50%.\nTest case 333: Chef can charge the battery for 151515 minutes and use it for 111 minute.\nThus, after 161616 minutes, the battery will be 50%50\\%50% .\nTest case 444: Chef can charge the battery for 252525 minutes to reach the battery level of 50%50\\%50%."
      }
    ]
  },
